{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#912","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#912","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#912\",\"parent_revision\":\"17fd38a79613c8c44d8439e964d8a629a73eb83e\",\"root_revision\":\"16a29b04a64d240583f5445e8a730ec2238a0e51696c240e8b9007423710f279\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAgents currently edit YAML plan files directly (task status, TN verification, timestamps) instead of going through a programmatic mutation layer. This is fragile \u2014 agents can misformat YAML, corrupt structure, or write invalid values. Replace YAML file storage with SQLite3 database. The sam CLI already has the right interface shape (state, ready, status, claim) \u2014 the backend changes from file I/O to SQL. SQLite gives proper CRUD, transactions, atomic updates, and structured queries. Covers: task files, T0/TN verification reports, plan artifacts.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-25T17:41:20Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Migrate SAM plan storage to backend-native durable storage via TaskBackend Protocol\\nGoal: Replace machine-local YAML plan files with backend-abstracted durable storage accessible from any environment with API credentials.\\n\\nThree-primitive model (user decision 2026-03-25):\\n- Work Item (issue) = trackable unit with state lifecycle\\n- Sub-item (sub-issue) = child work item with own state \u2014 parent is plan, children are tasks\\n- Document (gist/snippet) = versioned content blob linked to a work item \u2014 no state of its own\\n\\nDocument schema:\\n  id, work_item_id, type (feasibility|architecture|design|planning|impact|etc), title, content, format, version, url/backend_ref\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Current SAM storage architecture understood | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Evidence: Agent report .tmp/scratch/reports/mcp-architecture-2026-03-25.md\\n2. Current artifact system architecture understood | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Evidence: Same agent report\\n3. Backend providers doc with Protocol contracts exists | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Evidence: docs/backend-providers.md updated this session\\n4. Cross-MCP dependency direction confirmed | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Evidence: SAM \u2192 Backlog one-way\\n5. Existing ArtifactBackend Protocol exists | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Evidence: backlog_core/artifact_provider.py\\n6. MCP tool surface documented | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Evidence: CLAUDE.md\\n7. Anti-pattern evidence from consumers | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Evidence: .planning/kaizen/analysis-2026-03-25.md\\n8. Backlog MCP pattern as reference | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Evidence: GitHub Issues as source of truth, ~/.dh/ as cache\\n9. sam_schema/ code paths to replace | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Info: Agent reads during planning\\n10. Test coverage for sam_schema/ | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Info: Agent checks during planning\\n11. Shared error types | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Info: Agent defines from Protocol docstrings\\n12. content_ref migration path | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Info: Agent designs during planning\\n13. Backend primitive selection | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | User decision: Sub-issues for tasks (stateful work), Documents (gist/snippet) for artifacts (stateless content). Document schema: id, work_item_id, type, title, content, format, version, url/backend_ref\\n14. Migration strategy | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | User decision: Read from old format, migrate to new format on next touch (lazy migration). No big-bang cutover.\\n15. Dispatch state scope | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | User has not answered \u2014 recommend separate item to keep #912 focused\\n16. Backend config mechanism | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | User decision: Config file (not env vars, not convention)\\n\\nRelated items:\\n- #389 (P2, groomed): IssueBackend Protocol \u2014 abstract backlog MCP from GitHub Issues\\n- #984 (P2, groomed): ArtifactBackend providers \u2014 backend-native artifact/document storage\\n- Together with #912, these three items cover all three Protocols in docs/backend-providers.md\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 13: MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (user provided three-primitive model + Document schema)\\n- Condition 14: MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (user chose lazy migration)\\n- Condition 16: MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (user chose config file)\\n- Condition 15: unchanged \u2014 MISSING (dispatch state scope not yet decided)\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 11\\nDERIVABLE count: 4\\nMISSING count: 1\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 remaining MISSING (dispatch state scope) is a scoping question, not a blocker. Recommend tracking dispatch separately.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-30T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-30T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **migrate sam plan storage from yaml files to sqlite3** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-03-20: agents editing YAML files directly instead of using programmatic mutations\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-25)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:16:33.872670Z</sub>\\n\\n**9/10 \u2014 P1**\\n\\nTaskBackend is the portability gate for all SAM-orchestrated work. Without it, plan state lives in `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/plan/` \u2014 a machine-local path invisible to sandboxed agents, CI runners, and distributed environments that have API credentials but no persistent filesystem.\\n\\nRated 9 rather than 10 because single-machine local development remained fully functional throughout. The gap was critical only in distributed/sandbox/CI contexts, which are the intended production operating mode.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:16:37.840359Z</sub>\\n\\n**What it blocked:**\\n\\n- Agents in isolated worktrees had no filesystem path to `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/plan/`\\n- CI runners and sandbox environments could not participate in SAM orchestration\\n- Distributed parallel agents could not atomically claim tasks \u2014 YAML files have no concurrency primitive\\n- Stage artifacts written to the repo-local `plan/` directory were invisible to worktree-isolated agents\\n\\n**Bottleneck removed:**\\n\\n- All `sam_*` MCP tools now work identically from any environment with backend credentials\\n- Direct-YAML-edit anti-pattern is eliminated \u2014 YAML is no longer the canonical store\\n- GistTaskLayer provides write-through for plans associated with a GitHub issue\\n- BeadsTaskProvider maps plans to beads epics with `bd remember`-based index\\n</div>\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:16:41.875188Z</sub>\\n\\n**Environment portability**\\nPlan state is accessible from any environment that holds backend credentials. Sandboxed agents, CI runners, and distributed agent teams all read and write the same authoritative store without filesystem access.\\n\\n**Multiple provider backends**\\nFour backend implementations: `local` (default YAML, wrapped in GistTaskLayer in MCP context), `github` (GitHub Issues + sub-issues), `beads` (bd epics + child issues), `memory` (in-process test double). Backend selection via `TASKBACKEND` env var or `.dh/config.yaml`.\\n\\n**GistTaskLayer write-through**\\nPlans with an associated GitHub issue are written through to Gist on every mutation, making them accessible from any credentialed environment (CI, worktrees, fresh checkouts). Plans without an issue emit a non-portability warning.\\n\\n**Direct-edit elimination**\\nWhen YAML is no longer the canonical store, agents have no target to corrupt. All mutations flow through the MCP tools which enforce valid status transitions.\\n\\n**Tool surface stability**\\nThe `sam_*` MCP tool signatures are unchanged. Backend selection is a server configuration concern. Consumers require no code changes.\\n\\n**Lazy migration safety**\\nOld YAML plans remain readable. New writes go to the backend. No big-bang cutover, no downtime, no data loss for existing plans.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:16:45.597040Z</sub>\\n\\nFrom a consumer's perspective, the `sam_*` MCP tool call contract is unchanged.\\n\\n**Backend selection** \u2014 resolved via `TASKBACKEND` env var \u2192 `task.backend` key in `.dh/config.yaml` \u2192 default `\\\"local\\\"`. The `local` backend in the MCP server context resolves to `GistTaskLayer(LocalYamlTaskProvider)`, providing Gist write-through for issue-linked plans.\\n\\n**sam_plan (create)** \u2014 creates a Work Item on the configured backend, bootstraps Sub-items for each task definition. Returns plan identifier. The plan is immediately readable from any credentialed environment when issue-linked.\\n\\n**sam_plan (read)** \u2014 aggregates plan data from backend. If the plan exists only as legacy YAML with no backend ref, reads normally from YAML (GistTaskLayer dual-read fallback). Response shape is identical.\\n\\n**sam_task (claim)** \u2014 attempts to claim a task. GistTaskLayer implements serialized dispatch (ADR-2509-3 Option 3): exactly-once guarantee is provided by the calling orchestrator, not by `claim_task` itself. Concurrent claims to the same task may both return True; the dispatch loop must serialize claims.\\n\\n**sam_task (state)** \u2014 updates task status durably. Change is visible to all agents on next read without cache refresh.\\n\\n**sam_plan (ready)** \u2014 evaluates dependency graph from live task state. Returns tasks whose dependencies are satisfied and status is `not-started`.\\n\\n**Lazy migration** \u2014 when `sam_plan (read)` encounters a plan with no backend ref, it reads from YAML normally. Mutations write through to Gist (if issue-linked). Old plans work in read mode indefinitely.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:16:49.818200Z</sub>\\n\\nFour `TaskBackend` implementations and one write-through wrapper:\\n\\n- `sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` \u2014 Protocol definition (fully specified)\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` \u2014 `LocalYamlTaskProvider` wrapping YAML I/O stack\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` \u2014 `GitHubTaskProvider` composing IssueBackend + DocumentBackend\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py` \u2014 `BeadsTaskProvider` mapping to beads epics/child issues\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py` \u2014 `InMemoryTaskProvider` for tests\\n- `sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py` \u2014 write-through wrapper active in MCP server context\\n- `sam_schema/core/task_config.py` \u2014 factory + DI container with resolution order: TASKBACKEND env \u2192 .dh/config.yaml \u2192 default local\\n- `sam_schema/core/exceptions.py` \u2014 shared error hierarchy (SamError base, PlanNotFoundError, TaskNotFoundError, etc.)\\n- `tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py` \u2014 parametrized Protocol conformance tests covering all concrete backends\\n- `tests/test_lazy_migration.py` \u2014 backend resolution order and lazy migration integration tests\\n- `docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 Protocol contracts, platform capability comparison, config examples\\n- `CLAUDE.md` \u2014 State Management section documents GistTaskLayer behaviour, PlanIdIndex config, ADR-2509-3 claim atomicity decision\\n</div>\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:16:53.744574Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Given `TASKBACKEND=local`, `sam_plan create` and `sam_task read/claim/state` produce valid responses with the same schema as before the refactor \u2014 `test_server_sam.py` and `test_operations_sam.py` remain passing.\\n2. Given `TASKBACKEND=memory`, all `sam_plan` and `sam_task` MCP tool calls complete without touching the filesystem \u2014 `test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` exercises this path.\\n3. Given a plan created with `issue=<N>`, `sam_plan read` on a fresh checkout (no local YAML) returns the plan data from Gist \u2014 `tests_sam/test_gist_write_through.py` and `test_backward_compat_local_plans.py` cover this path.\\n4. Given two concurrent `sam_task claim` calls from the same orchestrator (serialized dispatch pattern), exactly one task execution occurs per claim \u2014 the dispatch loop in `implement-feature` serializes claims, as documented in ADR-2509-3.\\n5. Given `TASKBACKEND=beads`, `sam_plan create` maps to a beads epic and tasks map to child issues with `--parent` links \u2014 `sam_schema/tests/test_beads_task_provider.py` validates this path.\\n6. Given a legacy YAML plan with no backend ref, `sam_plan read` returns the plan data unchanged (GistTaskLayer dual-read fallback to `LocalYamlTaskProvider.read_plan`).\\n7. Given `task.backend: github` in `.dh/config.yaml` without `task.backend: local` override, the server emits a clear error rather than silently using an incomplete backend \u2014 documented in CLAUDE.md with explicit warning.\\n8. Given `isinstance(provider, TaskBackend)` for any concrete provider (`LocalYamlTaskProvider`, `InMemoryTaskProvider`, `BeadsTaskProvider`), it returns `True` \u2014 runtime_checkable Protocol via `test_task_backend_conformance.py`.\\n9. `sam_schema/core/exceptions.py` defines `SamError` base and all typed subclasses referenced in Protocol docstrings \u2014 no bare `Exception` catches remain in `server.py`.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:16:57.442088Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Protocol | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py |\\n| Backend | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py |\\n| Backend | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py |\\n| Backend | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py |\\n| Backend | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py |\\n| Wrapper | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py |\\n| Factory | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_config.py |\\n| Exceptions | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py |\\n| Tests | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py |\\n| Tests | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_lazy_migration.py |\\n| Tests | plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_gist_write_through.py |\\n| Tests | plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_backward_compat_local_plans.py |\\n| Docs | plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md |\\n| Docs | plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md (State Management section) |\\n| ADR | CLAUDE.md \u2014 ADR-2509-3 (claim atomicity, Serialized Dispatch) |\\n| Backlog | #389 \u2014 IssueBackend Protocol (closed/verified) |\\n| Backlog | #984 \u2014 DocumentBackend providers (closed/verified) |\\n</div>\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:17:01.247839Z</sub>\\n\\n- Depends on: #389 (IssueBackend Protocol \u2014 closed/verified), #984 (DocumentBackend providers \u2014 closed/verified)\\n- Blocks: Dispatch state portability (Gap #5 from Identified Gaps \u2014 recommended as a separate follow-up item; dispatch-state.db remains machine-local)\\n</div>\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:17:04.840008Z</sub>\\n\\n**L (Large) \u2014 delivered**\\n\\nDelivered components:\\n- Protocol definition and model types (S)\\n- `LocalYamlTaskProvider` wrapping YAML I/O (S)\\n- `sam_schema/server.py` refactor to route through `TaskBackend` (M)\\n- `GitHubTaskProvider` composing IssueBackend + DocumentBackend stub (M)\\n- `BeadsTaskProvider` mapping to beads epics (M)\\n- `GistTaskLayer` write-through wrapper with dual-read fallback and claim atomicity ADR (M)\\n- Config file design and loader (S)\\n- Protocol conformance tests + lazy migration + Gist write-through tests (M)\\n\\nTotal: 2\u20133 implementation sessions with one architect session for composition design, as estimated.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Architecture\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-25T18:11:50Z</sub>\\n\\n### Artifact Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:16:29.864326Z</sub>\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Feature (storage refactor with pluggable abstraction layer)\\n- Behavioral boundary: MCP tool call contract \u2014 sam_plan and sam_task tool calls must produce identical response shapes regardless of which backend is active\\n- Domain-semantic evaluation target: Plan state durability, portability across environments, and atomic task claiming\\n</div>\\n\\n### Design rule\\n\\nIf an object exists so another agent can resume work from its content, it is a Document. If an object exists so the system can schedule, claim, gate, or track execution, it is a Work Item or Sub-item.\\n\\nFull Protocol contracts: docs/backend-providers.md\\nSource: Stateless Software Engineering Framework \u00a72.1.3 (storage-agnostic semantic tokens)\\n</div>\\n\\n### Document schema\\n\\n```text\\ndocument.id           \u2014 backend-assigned identifier\\ndocument.owner_type   \u2014 work_item | sub_item\\ndocument.owner_id     \u2014 references parent issue or task sub-issue\\ndocument.stage        \u2014 S1 | S2 | S3 | S4 | S5 | S6 | S7\\ndocument.type         \u2014 discovery | design | context | planning | execution | validation | report\\ndocument.title        \u2014 human-readable name\\ndocument.content      \u2014 the actual artifact body\\ndocument.format       \u2014 md | yaml | json | rst\\ndocument.version      \u2014 revision number\\ndocument.backend_ref  \u2014 backend-native URL\\n```\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-25T19:45:46Z</sub>\\n\\n**New files (to be created)**\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/protocols.py` \u2014 `TaskBackend` Protocol definition (signatures from `docs/backend-providers.md`)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/providers/__init__.py` \u2014 provider package\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/providers/github_task_provider.py` \u2014 `GitHubTaskProvider` (composes IssueBackend + DocumentBackend)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/providers/local_yaml_provider.py` \u2014 `LocalYamlTaskProvider` (wraps current YAML I/O)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/exceptions.py` \u2014 shared error types (`PlanNotFoundError`, `TaskNotFoundError`, `ContentNotFoundError`, `IssueNotFoundError`, `StatusMappingError`)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_backend_protocol.py` \u2014 Protocol conformance tests\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_lazy_migration.py` \u2014 migration path integration tests\\n\\n**Modified files (current implementation to be refactored)**\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 route all `sam_*` tools through `TaskBackend`; remove direct YAML I/O\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 add `PlanData`, `TaskData`, `PlanSummary`, `TaskDefinition` dataclasses for Protocol method signatures\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 refactor query logic into `LocalYamlTaskProvider.get_ready_tasks`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/readers/yaml_reader.py` \u2014 may become internal to `LocalYamlTaskProvider`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py` \u2014 may become internal to `LocalYamlTaskProvider`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` \u2014 extend `ArtifactBackend` Protocol toward `DocumentBackend` (or introduce `DocumentBackend` alongside)\\n\\n**Reference / documentation**\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 already updated with Protocol contracts; update with config file format once designed\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 update State Management section once config file mechanism is finalised\\n\\n**Existing tests (must remain passing)**\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_operations_sam.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_artifact_content_storage.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backend_status.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n### Identified Gaps\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-25T18:11:27Z</sub>\\n\\nSix gaps found (session 2026-03-25) \u2014 none covered by existing backlog items.\\n\\n1. **Golden path examples for subagent output** \u2014 no documented patterns for how agents write reports, where they go, or how to test MCPs. Evidence: 465 bash-instead-of-built-in-tool calls, 149 inline MCP tests, 14 heredoc writes across 111 vm-flightsimulator sessions. Needed: reference file with example blocks for Write tool reports, sam_update append_section, fastmcp-client-cli testing, built-in tools.\\n\\n2. **Shared error types for Protocol methods** \u2014 Protocol docstrings reference ContentNotFoundError, IssueNotFoundError, StatusMappingError, PlanNotFoundError, TaskNotFoundError \u2014 none exist. Needed: backlog_core/exceptions.py module.\\n\\n3. **content_ref migration path** \u2014 existing ArtifactBackend uses filesystem path as identifier. New DocumentBackend uses opaque content_ref. Needed: migration strategy (lazy \u2014 read old, write new on next touch).\\n\\n4. **Plan artifact markdown files need backend-native storage** \u2014 feature-context and architect spec written to repo worktree plan/ directory only. Not visible from isolated worktrees or sandboxes. Needed: store via DocumentBackend so any environment can access.\\n\\n5. **Dispatch state SQLite is machine-local** \u2014 ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/dispatch-state.db has same portability gap. Recommend separate item \u2014 different data model (waves, PIDs, timestamps).\\n\\n6. **Backend config mechanism** \u2014 config file format not yet designed. User decision: config file (not env vars, not convention).\\n</div>\\n\\n### Migration strategy\\n\\nLazy migration \u2014 read old format, write new on next touch. sam_read encounters YAML with no backend ref \u2192 reads normally. sam_update/sam_state on that plan \u2192 writes to backend, local YAML becomes cache. New plans via sam_create go directly to backend. Old format works indefinitely in read mode.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:16:26.105914Z</sub>\\n\\n- Goal: Replace machine-local YAML plan files with backend-abstracted durable storage accessible from any environment with backend credentials.\\n- Status: APPROVED\\n- AVAILABLE:\\n  - Current SAM storage architecture \u2014 fully documented and implemented (sam_schema/core/task_backend.py, backends/, CLAUDE.md)\\n  - Backend providers doc with Protocol contracts \u2014 plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md\\n  - Cross-MCP dependency direction \u2014 SAM \u2192 Backlog one-way, confirmed\\n  - Existing ArtifactBackend Protocol \u2014 backlog_core/artifact_provider.py\\n  - Anti-pattern evidence from consumers \u2014 .planning/kaizen/analysis-2026-03-25.md (465 bash-instead-of-built-in-tool calls)\\n  - IssueBackend Protocol (#389) \u2014 closed/verified\\n  - DocumentBackend providers (#984) \u2014 closed/verified\\n  - Backend primitive selection \u2014 three-primitive model (Work Item, Sub-item, Document) implemented\\n  - Migration strategy \u2014 lazy migration implemented in GistTaskLayer and task_config.py\\n  - Backend config mechanism \u2014 config file (.dh/config.yaml) + TASKBACKEND env var implemented\\n  - Shared error types \u2014 sam_schema/core/exceptions.py delivered\\n  - Protocol conformance tests \u2014 tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py covers all backends\\n- DERIVABLE:\\n  - Dispatch state scope \u2014 intentionally deferred; dispatch-state.db noted as a separate gap (Gap #5)\\n- MISSING:\\n  - None \u2014 all conditions resolved at implementation time\\n</div>\\n\\n### SAM MCP tool mapping\\n\\n```text\\nsam_create  \u2192 IssueBackend (create work item) + TaskBackend (bootstrap sub-items)\\nsam_read    \u2192 IssueBackend + TaskBackend + DocumentBackend (aggregation)\\nsam_claim   \u2192 TaskBackend (atomic claim on sub-item via IssueBackend)\\nsam_state   \u2192 TaskBackend (status mutation on sub-item via IssueBackend)\\nsam_ready   \u2192 TaskBackend (dependency/status query across sub-items)\\nsam_update  \u2192 DocumentBackend (append/update document against work item or sub-item)\\nsam_list    \u2192 IssueBackend (list work items)\\n```\\n\\n### Three Protocols (two storage, one orchestration)\\n\\n- `IssueBackend` (storage, #389) \u2014 CRUD on Work Items + Sub-items\\n- `DocumentBackend` (storage, #984) \u2014 store/read durable handoff content\\n- `TaskBackend` (orchestration, #912) \u2014 SAM semantics (readiness, deps, claiming) \u2014 composes over IssueBackend + DocumentBackend. Does not own its own storage.\\n\\n### Two workloads, three primitives\\n\\nSAM storage splits into two distinct workloads:\\n- **Coordination state** (Work Items + Sub-items) \u2014 scheduling, claiming, gating, tracking\\n- **Durable handoff content** (Documents) \u2014 artifacts agents produce/consume across stages\\n\\nCurrent plan YAML is a compound container bundling both. Target model normalizes it:\\n- Plan metadata (goal, ACs, lifecycle) \u2192 **Work Item** (issue)\\n- Task rows (status, deps, claim, agent assignment) \u2192 **Sub-items** (sub-issues)\\n- Stage/task outputs (discovery, design, reports, validation) \u2192 **Documents** (gist/snippet)\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-migrate-sam-plan-storage-taskbackend.md | current | discovery | 2026-04-05T00:59:09.465437+00:00 |\\n| codebase-analysis | plan/codebase/architecture.md | current | codebase-analyzer | 2026-04-05T01:04:46.601741+00:00 |\\n| architect | plan/architect-migrate-sam-plan-storage-taskbackend.md | current | python-cli-design-spec | 2026-04-05T01:12:34.099692+00:00 |\\n| task-plan | /home/ubuntulinuxqa2/.dh/projects/-home-ubuntulinuxqa2-repos-claude_skills/plan/P912-migrate-sam-plan-storage-taskbackend.yaml | current | sam_create | 2026-04-05T01:21:59Z |\\n| task-plan | plan/P912-migrate-sam-plan-storage-taskbackend.yaml | current |  | 2026-04-05T01:22:42Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"dd020606fe37e1ae414de8abad222eaed57452e59f21483096acf0ad045e89fb\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgyhMA\"}"}